<title>USA: Ravenswood Aluminum hikes plate prices.</title>
<headline>Ravenswood Aluminum hikes plate prices.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ravenswood Aluminum, wholly owned by Century Aluminum Co, said it will raise prices for heat-treated aluminum plate by 5 percent effective with orders received on or after March 4, and will all shipments on or after June 1, 1997.</p>
<p>The hike will come from eliminating discounts or by raising base prices.</p>
<p>The new prices cover plate products in alloys 2124, 7050, 7150, 7475, 2014, 2024, 2219, 7039, 7075, and 6061.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
